  "aim": {
    "cw": "Cut the Italian withdrawal route by reaching Beda Fomm and occupy Benghazi.",
    "axis": "Retain Benghazi and prevent a Commonwealth occupation of the port."
  },
  "about": "Linked research pursuit and road-block phase. The historical advance crossed from Mechili toward Msus and Antelat, blocked the coastal escape near Beda Fomm, and occupied Benghazi. The model uses a 10 km Beda Fomm hex as the blocking objective; it does not yet simulate the historical 5–7 February encirclement and mass surrender. Actual losses, ownership and stocks from the prior chapter carry forward. The copied placements and owners are checker placeholders; no separate historical start is claimed. A provisional 2,000-man Benghazi security counter is a game estimate so port control requires occupation; its identity and strength need documentary verification.",
  "sources": {
    "W": "Wavell, Western Desert operations despatch, London Gazette 37628, sections 10–21: plan, forces, opening, Nibeiwa and Sidi Barrani",
    "P": "Playfair et al., The Mediterranean and Middle East, vol. I, chapter XIV: positions, supply preparation, assault sequence and withdrawal of 4th Indian Division",
    "A": "Australian official history, To Benghazi, chapter 6: Commonwealth formations and armoured screening task",
    "E": "Game estimate: individual-unit strength, exact 10 km placement, opening stock or supply setting not verified by the cited account",
    "B": "Australian official history, To Benghazi, chapter VII Before Bardia: 16th Brigade via Buq Buq and Sollum 17-19 December; 17th Brigade and divisional HQ move ordered for 22 December; 19th Brigade forward 1 January",
    "P2": "Playfair et al., The Mediterranean and Middle East, vol. I, chapter XV: Sollum port and supply, Bardia perimeter preparations, ammunition delay and 7th RTR serviceability",
    "O": "6th Australian Division operation order, 1 January 1941, Appendix 2 of Australian official history To Benghazi: western attack, phases, 7th RTR and 17th Brigade",
    "H": "Australian War Memorial Battle of Bardia: breach 3 January, town 4 January, southern surrender 5 January",
    "T": "Australian official history, To Benghazi, chapter 9: XXII Corps, 61st Sirte and Tobruk garrison; approximately 25,000 men and 220 guns estimated 15 January",
    "T2": "Australian official history, To Benghazi, chapter 9: Bardia to Tobruk, XXII Corps garrison, preparation and attack on 21 January",
    "P3": "UK official history, The Mediterranean and Middle East vol I chapter XV: Tobruk garrison, routes, preparations and fall",
    "D": "Australian official history, To Benghazi, chapter 10, The Engagement at Derna: 22 January advance, Derna rearguard and 30 January occupation; contemporary estimate of 60th Sabratha and Babini armour near Derna/Mechili. Exact strength and scenario-entry placement remain unverified.",
    "F": "Australian official history, To Benghazi, chapter 11, Beda Fomm and Benghazi: 3 February withdrawal, 4 February desert march, 5–7 February road block and surrender, and the Benghazi occupation."
  },
